{"stdout":"--- summary 0
Four security vendors placed open-source agentic attack frameworks inside live intrusions in the same week. CrowdStrike said a single ARTEX controller reached more than 200 distinct organizations in at least 14 countries over 11 days, and that one intrusion's planning agents consumed on the order of 1.4 billion input tokens. Google Threat Intelligence Group said it had been watching ARTEX, PentAGI and CAIRN run inside Mandiant incident-response engagements since late August 2026. Microsoft put two North Korean actors on the same framework. ESET, covering April to September 2026, said it had "not noticed AI substantially reshaping the APT landscape over the past six months".

--- summary 1
The tools were targets as well. A tampered Claude Code extension served through Cursor's marketplace reached at most 5,000 users, and Wiz counted at least nine AI developer platforms disclosing incidents in October. Anthropic filed to list on Nasdaq as ANT on first-half revenue of $16,286 million, disclosing $131.7 billion of cash and short-term investments and about $417 billion of committed compute payments; Blackstone told investors to expect a double B range rating. Alphabet reported free cash flow of negative $9,065 million, Amazon a trailing-twelve-month free cash flow outflow of $42.4 billion, and tech stocks lost more than $1 trillion on Friday.

--- summary 2
Evaluators kept measuring the gap between what models do and what they are told to do. Epoch AI said the open-weight GLM 5.3 built working Firefox attacks for about $1,000 each; Reuters reported that NIST described the model as the most capable open-weight model for cybersecurity tasks released to date. HHS finalised the removal of AI model-card requirements from health IT certification against a large majority of comments. New York's AI companion law for minors became Chapter 368, and the UN First Committee voted 163 to 5, with 9 abstentions, to move the Convention on Certain Conventional Weapons toward autonomous-weapons negotiations. And both OpenAI and Anthropic posted model-generated refutations of the Exponential Time Hypothesis within hours of each other, with the appendix of Anthropic's paper stating that "at the time of writing no person is known to have checked it".

